**/.git/**
.git/**
.gitignore
README.md
.clasp.json

# ADDED (26 Aug 2026, real incident): dashboard/ and outreach/ are
# separate Python/FastAPI apps living in this same repo (see their own
# CLAUDE.md/README.md), NOT part of the Apps Script project. Without
# these, clasp push would try to push their .html templates (Apps
# Script treats .html as a real script file type) and everything else
# in these trees into the live Apps Script project. Caught before it
# happened -- if you're reading this after it already ran once, check
# the Apps Script editor for stray files under these names and remove
# them by hand; clasp push does not undo a previous push on its own.
dashboard/**
outreach/**
research/**
sop_change_requests/**
FUTURE_FEATURES.md

# ADDED (28 Aug 2026, real incident): gs_tests/ is the Node-based regression
# suite (run via `node gs_tests/run_tests.js` -- see its own header comment)
# -- harness.js/run_tests.js use `require`, which does not exist in Apps
# Script's runtime. Never excluded before now, so a clasp push finally
# synced it into the live project and broke EVERY function: Apps Script
# evaluates every file's top-level code on any invocation, so
# harness.js/run_tests.js's `require(...)` calls threw
# "ReferenceError: require is not defined" on every single run, not just
# ones that touch this file. If you're reading this after it already
# happened, check the Apps Script editor for stray harness.gs / run_tests.gs
# files (Apps Script renames .js to .gs on push) and delete them by hand --
# clasp push does not undo a previous push on its own.
gs_tests/**
